<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-eusthenopteron-foordi-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing k_c at 104 µm on Eusthenopteron foordi (Frasnian, 379 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 81.2/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Schnakenberg kinetics with the Turing wavenumber set so λ_c = 104.2 µm. Pass 1 confirms the integrator runs, the Brussels mount is the display domain, and the realized wavelength is 102.0 µm. Sweep monotonicity, ablation stds, mask morphometrics, and the dispersion residual are listed as remediation rather than fully credited. Overall 81.2/100 (faithfulness 79.4, reproducibility 85.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 76, Parameter expressivity 74, Morphometric validation 80, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/eusthenopteron_foordi_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-eusthenopteron-foordi-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 631334 B, 1584×888 px, artifact_sha256 721d8d4672825d003f90b6fdfb105ec4274bfb531a752756f483adad178cf1c5 (sha256 721d8d4672825d003f90b6fdfb105ec4274bfb531a752756f483adad178cf1c5), spec_fingerprint 7d5c5c4a83fa8f6c063e1e197796aa4e97931ea29ced33c300363ee59ac62e99. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 7d5c5c4a83fa8f6c063e1e197796aa4e97931ea29ced33c300363ee59ac62e99; artifact_sha256: 721d8d4672825d003f90b6fdfb105ec4274bfb531a752756f483adad178cf1c5. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical wavenumber | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics | Kondo and Asai 1995 dermal pigment waves on living fish | Andrews and Westoll 1970 osteology of Eusthenopteron foordi; reconstructed_in_script: Dv/Du = 12 chosen so formula k_c = 2π per 104.2 µm | Fourier integration on a 12 by 7.5 wavelength patch; transfer_boundary: Teleost chromatophore RD applied to a 379 Ma tristichopterid dermis | 104.2 µm is the assigned detail scale, not a histological count on this fossil; does_not_claim: Preserved chromatophore color on the Brussels mount | A calibrated micrometre scale bar in the photograph." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Goodness-of-fit: Pearson r, RMSE on σ(k), and the KS/CV specimen comparison must be the morphometric evidence, with value ≠ reference.",
        "remediation needed: Negative control and ablation: report equal-diffusion std and autocatalysis-ablated std beside the patterned std.",
        "remediation needed: Parameter-regime sweep: re-score Dv/Du against realized wavelength, including the near-threshold ratio and the non-monotone step.",
        "remediation needed: Real specimen CV segmentation: score the body mask (aspect, circularity) against the gallery reconstruction and record the orientation KS." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.12e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

