<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-eusthenopteron-foordi-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Turing k_c at 104 µm on Eusthenopteron foordi (Frasnian, 379 Ma) (Eusthenopteron foordi)",
        "Turing k_c at 104 µm on Eusthenopteron foordi (Frasnian, 379 Ma) faithfully reproduces Eusthenopteron foordi morphology" ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-eusthenopteron-foordi-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Eusthenopteron foordi specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-eusthenopteron-foordi-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Eusthenopteron foordi" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A calibrated micrometre scale bar in the photograph",
        "does_not_claim: Preserved chromatophore color on the Brussels mount",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Dv/Du = 12 chosen so formula k_c = 2π per 104.2 µm",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Fourier integration on a 12 by 7.5 wavelength patch",
        "reported_in_source: Andrews and Westoll 1970 osteology of Eusthenopteron foordi",
        "reported_in_source: Kondo and Asai 1995 dermal pigment waves on living fish",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical wavenumber",
        "transfer_boundary: 104.2 µm is the assigned detail scale, not a histological count on this fossil",
        "transfer_boundary: Teleost chromatophore RD applied to a 379 Ma tristichopterid dermis" ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Eusthenopteron foordi (Late Devonian (Frasnian, 379 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Pisces (Ichthyes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Eusthenopteron" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-eusthenopteron-foordi-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/eusthenopteron_foordi_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Eusthenopteron foordi; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical wavenumber | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics | Kondo and Asai 1995 dermal pigment waves on living fish | Andrews and Westoll 1970 osteology of Eusthenopteron foordi; reconstructed_in_script: Dv/Du = 12 chosen so formula k_c = 2π per 104.2 µm | Fourier integration on a 12 by 7.5 wavelength patch; transfer_boundary: Teleost chromatophore RD applied to a 379 Ma tristichopterid dermis | 104.2 µm is the assigned detail scale, not a histological count on this fossil; does_not_claim: Preserved chromatophore color on the Brussels mount | A calibrated micrometre scale bar in the photograph]; phenomenon_size: 113 µm (0.0001131 m, log10=-3.947 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 113 µm to 25.4 cm): 113 µm:eusthenopteron-foordi-bioelectric-polarity, 354 µm:eusthenopteron-foordi-vertex-packing, 5.7 mm:eusthenopteron-foordi-turing-wavelength, 1.1 cm:eusthenopteron-foordi-clock-wavefront, 2.5 cm:eusthenopteron-foordi-morphogen-condensation, 3.1 cm:eusthenopteron-foordi-elastic-buckling, 3.5 cm:eusthenopteron-foordi-flux-canalization, 4.9 cm:eusthenopteron-foordi-branching-tree" ;
